---
import benchmark from '../generated/benchmark.json';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { repository } from '../lib/site';
const { results, maxTime, minimumSaved, maximumSaved } = benchmark;
const evidence = `${repository}/blob/${benchmark.evidenceCommit}/${benchmark.dataset}`;
const advantage = (saved: number) => `${Math.abs(saved).toFixed(1)}% ${saved >= 0 ? 'less' : 'more'} time`;
---
<section class="home-performance" aria-labelledby="performance-heading">
  <div class="home-performance-summary">
    <div class="home-performance-title"><h2 id="performance-heading">The export, measured.</h2><p>Rust Project API versus genanki 0.13.1 · {benchmark.notes.toLocaleString('en-US')} Basic notes per workload</p></div>
    <div class="home-performance-metric"><strong>{results[0].rust.toFixed(1)}<span> ms</span></strong><span>Text-only export</span></div>
    {minimumSaved >= 0 && <div class="home-performance-metric"><strong>{minimumSaved.toFixed(1)}–{maximumSaved.toFixed(1)}<span>%</span></strong><span>Less export time across five measured workloads</span></div>}
  </div>
  <p class="home-performance-context">Rust Project API · Media::files · commit {benchmark.measurementCommit.slice(0, 7)} · Apple M1 Pro · 10-run medians · 2026-10-08</p>
  <div class="home-benchmark" data-reveal>
    <div class="home-benchmark-intro"><h3>Five kinds of input.<br />One reproducible comparison.</h3><p>Export times include process startup through exit. Every row contains {benchmark.notes.toLocaleString('en-US')} Basic notes; media content changes by workload.</p></div>
    <div class="home-benchmark-chart" aria-label="Median export times in milliseconds">
      <div class="home-benchmark-key"><span><i class="home-key-rust"></i>Anki Forge Rust</span><span><i class="home-key-genanki"></i>genanki</span></div>
      {results.map(result => <div class="home-benchmark-row" data-profile={result.profile} style={`--rust-width: ${result.rust / maxTime * 100}%; --genanki-width: ${result.genanki / maxTime * 100}%`}>
        <div class="home-benchmark-label"><span>{result.label}</span><strong>{advantage(result.saved)}</strong></div>
        <div class="home-benchmark-bars" aria-hidden="true"><span class="home-rust-bar"></span><span class="home-genanki-bar"></span></div>
        <p>{result.rust.toFixed(1)} ms <span>/ {result.genanki.toFixed(1)} ms</span></p>
      </div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="home-benchmark-footnote"><p>Some media workloads use more memory; the unique-image workload used 92.45 MiB peak RSS versus 35.59 MiB. These results measure committed source, independently of the public 0.2.0 packages.</p></div>
  </div>
  <details class="benchmark-method"><summary>Method, memory tradeoffs, and full results</summary>
    <p>Five workloads × 100 / 200 / 500 / 1,000 notes; 10 timing runs and 5 independent peak-RSS measurements per cell. Startup-to-exit time includes media import, build, inspection and writing.</p>
    <p>Apple M1 Pro / 32 GiB / macOS 27; Rust 1.92 release, default features, System allocator; CPython 3.11 / genanki 0.13.1. Default APKG formats differ. Background load and page cache were not isolated.</p>
    <table><caption>Peak RSS medians at {benchmark.notes.toLocaleString('en-US')} notes (MiB)</caption><thead><tr><th>Workload</th><th>Rust</th><th>genanki</th><th>Speed ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody>{results.map(result => <tr><th scope="row">{result.label}</th><td>{result.rustRSS.toFixed(2)}</td><td>{result.genankiRSS.toFixed(2)}</td><td>{result.speedup.toFixed(2)}×</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    <p>All 840 output-content checks and 40 Anki import, content and representative-render checks passed (20 imports per implementation). Across the full 20-cell matrix, Rust medians were lower and Rust Q3 was below genanki Q1. This does not certify every client.</p>
    <p>Node/Python hosts, prepared publication, repeated builds within one process and individual media over 1 MiB were not measured. GUI interaction and audible playback were not checked.</p>
    <p><a href={`${evidence}/report.md`}>Full time and RSS report <Icon name="arrowUpRight" /></a> · <a href={`${evidence}/comparison.csv`}>Raw CSV</a> · <a href={`${evidence}/measured-source-check.json`}>Measured source</a> · <a href={`${evidence}/README.md`}>Reproduce</a></p>
  </details>
</section>
